Verification Memo: Item 048 - Block B Plant-Room Excavation

To: Rachel Marlbeck
From: A. Vance
Date: 07/20/2026
Subject: Kesterline Shoring Design Verification

Basis of Verification:
- Current revision (Rev.2) of Item 048 (KE-L-2026-0713) was reviewed against logged groundwater levels (12.5 ft) and subsurface conditions (clay layer at 15 ft, no significant voids).
- Design checks for lateral earth pressure (12.5 kPa), hydrostatic pressure (8.2 kPa), and settlement (≤0.5 in) were cross-referenced with site data. Safety factors (FS=2.5) were verified against soil bearing capacity (15 kPa) and groundwater pressure (8.2 kPa).

Findings:
1. **Validated Checks**: Lateral earth pressure and settlement calculations align with standards. Hydrostatic pressure margins are sufficient.
2. **Pending**: Groundwater control measures (dewatering pumps) require confirmation from geotechnical team.

Disposition:
- Rev.2 design is acceptable for excavation, pending dewatering plan approval.
- Excavation can proceed on 08/10/2026 only after:
  - Finalized dewatering plan (submit by 07/28/2026)
  - Soil borings from Zone 3 (due 07/25/2026)

Impact on Permanent Work:
- Excavation will not interfere with existing foundations at Block B (10 ft below proposed excavation depth).

Status: Verified (open for dewatering plan submission)

A. Vance
Project Manager

